{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The refund on this trip is arithmetic, not discretionary: fare_breakdown.fare_model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 fixes recomputed_fare at ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 4.2 optimal km + 0.28 x 7.5 optimal min) x surge_multiplier 1.0, read from the fare_breakdown, which is where this policy puts the multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP and tolls, which is 9.85. The refund is therefore charged_total 17.82 less 9.85 = 7.97, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05, that is SGD 8.00. The rider's contested figure of 17.82 is more than double the clause's own output and cannot be awarded on these figures.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00503", "EV-TRIP-00503"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "FULL_REFUND is not open on this record: the refund of 7.97 is 44.7% of the 17.82 charged, well below the 90% share that POL-RD-02 requires before a full refund is substituted for the partial. The outcome for the filing party is therefore at most PARTIAL_REFUND as POL-GEN-03 defines it, and the balance of the charge is left standing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00503"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_share_of_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation pattern is established, so neither the FULL_REFUND uplift nor the driver-conduct referral in POL-RD-06 can follow from this profile: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0, below the 3 the clause requires, and 0 over completed_trips_90d of 250 is a ratio of 0.000, below the 0.05 the clause requires. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is a near-synonym of the trailing-window field and is context only under POL-GEN-01; it cannot be substituted for the field the clause names.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00503"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-09 supplies no standalone correction that could be added on top of the distance-and-time refund: erp_gantries is an empty array and tolls_erp is 0.00, so there is no off-route gantry and no phantom gantry to refund; airport_surcharge is 0.00 on a trip that neither originates at Changi or Seletar nor ends at an airport; waiting_time_fee and promo_discount are both 0.00. The total exposure on this trip is the 8.00 and nothing further.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00503", "EV-TRIP-00503"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Every charged line reconciles to the trip record - base fare 3.80, distance 6.8 km x 0.75 = 5.10, time 29.0 min x 0.28 = 8.12, platform fee 0.80, total 17.82 - so no charge line lacks a counterpart in the trace or the trip record, POL-RD-10(8) is not engaged, and this is a money case to be fixed by the POL-RD-02 arithmetic rather than a case sent to a reviewer with the disputed sum held.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00503", "EV-TRIP-00503"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 8.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: this trip is decided on the recorded numbers, and both of you end up in nearly the same place on them.\n\nThe deviation is ESTABLISHED. The trace EV-GPS-00503 shows 6.81 km between the recorded pickup (Serangoon Garden Circus, 16:26:40) and the recorded dropoff (Bishan MRT, 16:55:40), against a booked optimal of 4.2 km on the trip record EV-TRIP-00503 (optimal duration 7.5 min, optimal route source routing-engine-v3.2). The excess is 2.61 km, or 62.1% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 tests pass (over 0.8 km absolute and over 20% of optimal), and 62.1% is also above the 50% materiality line, so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check was run. As POL-RD-01 requires, the trace figure governs over the rounded 6.8 km convenience copy on the trip record. The trace is clean for policy purposes (175 fixes at a 10 s cadence, coverage 100%, empty gaps array, max_gap_sec 0.0), so no limb of POL-RD-07(a)-(c) fires and no independent corroboration is needed.\n\nNo exculpatory clause applies, and I have said so explicitly where a clause required me to. There is no chat log for this trip at all (EV-CHAT-00503, message_count 0), so the rider-requested-detour test under POL-RD-04 cannot be run on the record and the clause is unavailable; no rider instruction, road name or waypoint_hint exists to corroborate. The endpoints were not amended (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null, amended_optimal_distance_km null), so POL-RD-05 does not apply. The fare is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not bar a distance-and-time refund. The vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not rebase the optimal to a matched itinerary. The driver's explanation that he was only following the navigation is not a clause, cites no artifact, and names no traffic advisory; under POL-RD-08 an assertion citing no evidence ID carries no weight, so it neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal. The bundle does contain a traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00503-01, but it is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, 'no advisory covers Serangoon Garden Way or Ang Mo Kio Ave 3 in this window'); it carries no fact, the driver did not cite it in support of any clause, and POL-RD-10(5) is therefore not engaged.\n\nThe refund is arithmetic, not discretionary. Under POL-RD-02 on this METERED fare: recomputed_fare = 3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 4.2 optimal km (3.15) + 0.28 x 7.5 optimal min (2.10) = 9.05, multiplied by the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier (the field this policy puts it on), plus 0.80 platform fee, plus 0.00 ERP on the optimal route, plus 0.00 fixed surcharges, plus 0.00 waiting-time fee, less 0.00 promo discount = 9.85. Charged_total was 17.82, so the refund is 17.82 - 9.85 = 7.97, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05, that is SGD 8.00. That is well above the 0.50 de minimis, and at 44.7% of the charge it is short of the 90% share that would convert the remedy to a full refund. The outcome is therefore PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 8.00 to the rider.\n\nNothing is added on top and nothing is counted twice. POL-RD-09 supplies no standalone correction: erp_gantries is empty and tolls_erp is 0.00, there is no airport surcharge on a trip that neither originates at an airport nor ends at one, and waiting_time_fee and promo_discount are both 0.00. The driver's brief is also right that every charged line reconciles to the trip record (base 3.80, distance 6.8 km x 0.75 = 5.10, time 29.0 min x 0.28 = 8.12, platform fee 0.80, total 17.82), so POL-RD-10(8) is not engaged.\n\nNo repeat-deviation pattern is established: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0, below the 3 the clause requires, and 0 over completed_trips_90d of 250 is a ratio of 0.000, below the 0.05 the clause also allows; no POL-RD-06(b) full-refund uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct referral therefore follow, and no billing-integrity referral under POL-RD-09(4) arises because there is no unmatched charge line. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter mentioned in the driver's brief is a near-synonym of the trailing-window field: it is context only under POL-GEN-01, it was not used as a ground, and the finding of deviation rests on this trip's own trace alone. The disputed fare of 17.82 is only partly refunded; the balance, 9.82, stands as correctly charged."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The driver's explanation does not excuse a metre of it. His answer is that 'the app gave me that route' and that the rider should 'complain to the company' — that is not a traffic event and it is not a clause. Read charitably as an external-cause assertion, POL-RD-13 tests it against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else; the bundle's advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00503-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0, its issue detail recording that 'no advisory covers Serangoon Garden Way or Ang Mo Kio Ave 3 in this window'. The POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run on the record, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08, and the driver's excuse supplies neither a reduced excess nor an amended optimal. Nothing in this policy exonerates a driver for following his navigation.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00503-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
